@startuml E3-component-03-wallet-trades-layered
title CryptoWeb - Wallet and Market Trading Components (LAYERED)

!theme plain
left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam nodesep 110
skinparam ranksep 120
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam ArrowFontSize 11
hide stereotype

package "Server_3 :4000" {
  component "trade.controller.js" as S3Trade
  component "wallet.controller.js withdrawalBank.controller.js" as S3Wallet
  component "personA.gateway.js" as Gateway
  component "trade Mongoose model" as TradeProjection
}
package "Core :5000" {
  component "trade.controller.js" as CoreTradeCtrl
  component "trade.service.js" as CoreTradeSvc
  component "wallet.controller.js" as CoreWalletCtrl
  component "wallet.service.js" as CoreWalletSvc
  component "binancePrice.service.js" as PriceSvc
}
database "MySQL wallet / holding / trade fill" as SQL
database "MongoDB trades" as Mongo

S3Trade --> Gateway : execute trade
S3Wallet --> Gateway : wallet proxy
Gateway --> CoreTradeCtrl : REST
Gateway --> CoreWalletCtrl : REST
CoreTradeCtrl --> PriceSvc
CoreTradeCtrl --> CoreTradeSvc
CoreWalletCtrl --> CoreWalletSvc
CoreTradeSvc --> SQL : atomic settlement
CoreWalletSvc --> SQL : wallet operations
S3Trade --> TradeProjection : sync fill
TradeProjection --> Mongo

note bottom of CoreTradeSvc
Core commits the trade and wallet updates.
Server_3 subsequently writes a Mongo trade projection.
end note

@enduml
